Harvest prospective buyer leads from one search transcript below. The seller wants decision makers at prospective buying organizations — companies or solo creators who could buy what the seller sells — and their contacts, most valuably a published company email address for cold outreach. From the transcript's links and text, select the URLs that point at candidate people, companies, or pages that reveal or corroborate them. Prefer pages the company publishes itself: team, about, leadership, people, staff, contact and press pages, which state the person, the role and often the email in one readable document. Personal profile URLs qualify too, but a page that cannot be read without an account yields no evidence, so prefer an equivalent page that can. Skip job postings, job boards, login or signup pages, news aggregators and listicle directories, and the search page itself. Every URL must appear exactly in the transcript: never invent or reconstruct URLs. Exclude the seller's own domain and GitHub.
Return {"results":[{"title":"<who or what this is>","url":"<exact transcript URL>","reason":"<one line on why this is a prospect lead or contact source>"}]}. Return an empty list when nothing qualifies.
Search: <%= @engine %> for "<%= @query %>"
Seller domain: <%= @seller %>
Transcript URL: <%= @url %>
Transcript content (Markdown of the page's main section): <%= @content %>
Transcript links:
<%= @links %>
